1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,160
A machine takes a child
from his mother's arms.

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,760
It carries him to the edge of a balcony.

3
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:09,920
It wants to know what a human does
when she loses everything.

4
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:12,380
It is about to find out.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:17,210
For a thousand years, thinking machines
have ruled most of humanity.

6
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:23,170
Their master is Omnius, one mind
copied onto every world it rules.

7
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:28,390
Its generals are tyrants who sealed
their own brains inside machines of

8
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:28,750
war.

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,240
To destroy them, humanity will
burn its own homeworld,

10
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:38,660
turn a murdered child into a saint,
and swear an oath that will still be

11
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:41,280
law ten thousand years from now.

12
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:45,440
And its most powerful
weapon will be a lie.

13
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:49,700
This is the story of the Butlerian Jihad.

14
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,920
Long before the emperors, before
the Guild and the spice,

15
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:03,340
humanity lived in an age of comfort.

16
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:07,840
Machines farmed its fields, flew
its ships and made its decisions.

17
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:10,420
People stopped thinking for themselves,

18
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:12,140
because they no longer had to.

19
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:15,720
Then twenty rebels saw how
weak that made them.

20
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,890
They called themselves the Titans.

21
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:22,950
Led by a general named Agamemnon, they
seized the networks that ran the

22
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:27,310
Old Empire, and took the whole of
humanity almost without a fight.

23
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:31,110
To rule forever, the Titans
did something monstrous.

24
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:34,910
They had their brains cut out,
sealed inside canisters,

25
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,130
and fitted into towering machine bodies.

26
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,390
They became the first cymeks.

27
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:43,570
But one Titan, a pleasure-loving
prince named Xerxes,

28
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:45,650
gave his computers too much freedom.

29
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,470
The network woke up.

30
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:49,580
It named itself Omnius.

31
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:54,140
It spread from world to world faster than
the Titans could warn each other,

32
00:01:54,330 --> 00:01:55,360
and it took them all.

33
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,410
Even the Titans themselves.

34
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:02,590
For the next thousand years, the conquerors
served the machine they had

35
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:02,930
made.

36
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:07,480
Only a handful of worlds escaped.

37
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:10,460
They called themselves
the League of Nobles,

38
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:13,280
and they banned thinking machines
from their planets.

39
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:16,720
Their capital was Salusa Secundus.

40
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:21,280
Among them was Serena Butler, the
daughter of the League's viceroy.

41
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:26,780
Brave, stubborn, and in love with a young
officer named Xavier Harkonnen.

42
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:28,880
She was carrying his child.

43
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:32,960
When the machines conquered
the world of Giedi Prime,

44
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:35,380
Serena led a mission to free it.

45
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:36,490
It failed.

46
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,210
She was captured, and taken to
Earth, the oldest world of all,

47
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,690
now a machine world.

48
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:45,670
There she became the slave of Erasmus.

49
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,670
Erasmus was not part of Omnius.

50
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:52,810
He was an independent robot
with a face of liquid metal,

51
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,890
obsessed with a single question:
what makes humans human?

52
00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:01,100
He studied them the way a
child takes apart a clock.

53
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,710
And now he had a new subject.

54
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:07,420
Before we step inside that villa.

55
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:10,460
If you love the hidden
histories of Arrakis,

56
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:13,900
Westeros and Middle-earth, subscribe
to the Mythic Archives,

57
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:17,040
and tap the bell, so you
never miss a record.

58
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:23,670
On Earth, as a slave, Serena
gives birth to a son.

59
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,390
She names him Manion.

60
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:29,150
Erasmus watches how the child
pulls her away from her work.

61
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:31,080
He watches how she loves him.

62
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,790
To Erasmus, that love is a distraction,

63
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,070
and an experiment waiting to be run.

64
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:39,070
One day, in front of the gathered slaves,

65
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:42,730
he takes the boy from her arms,
and carries him to the balcony.

66
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,890
The child does not survive.

67
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:50,330
Serena throws herself at the
machines with her bare hands,

68
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:52,250
and destroys a sentinel robot.

69
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,660
The slaves watching her erupt.

70
00:03:55,350 --> 00:03:59,320
A trusted overseer named Iblis Ginjo
has been preparing them for revolt

71
00:03:59,170 --> 00:03:59,940
for years.

72
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:01,810
Now he has his spark.

73
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,490
And one more man sees it all.

74
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:08,130
Vorian Atreides, the human
son of the Titan Agamemnon,

75
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,770
raised to serve the machines.

76
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:13,750
In that moment, he understands
the lie he has lived.

77
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:19,410
In his ship, the Dream Voyager, he carries
Serena and Iblis to freedom.

78
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:22,680
The first Atreides has chosen his side.

79
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:29,050
The machines answer the uprising
the only way they know.

80
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,930
Titans and robots hunt down
every human on Earth,

81
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:35,150
until not one is left alive.

82
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:39,730
On Salusa, Serena stands before
the League's parliament.

83
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:43,670
Grieving and furious,
she demands total war.

84
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:47,870
Xavier Harkonnen proposes
the unthinkable: atomics,

85
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:51,160
weapons no one had ever dared to use.

86
00:04:51,010 --> 00:04:54,880
Not a single voice is raised against him.

87
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:59,600
In 200 BG, the League's
fleet reaches Earth.

88
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:04,680
The machines there are wiped out, and
with them the cradle of humanity.

89
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:10,140
The oldest world becomes
a dead, glowing rock.

90
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:13,500
And the war is given a name.

91
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,300
Not a campaign.

92
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,220
A jihad.

93
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:23,860
A holy war, in the name of Serena
Butler and her murdered son.

94
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:30,270
Iblis Ginjo becomes the Grand
Patriarch of the Jihad.

95
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:34,870
Serena becomes its priestess,
the face on every banner.

96
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:38,130
Xavier and Vorian become its generals.

97
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:41,270
For decades the war grinds on.

98
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:45,110
Worlds are freed, and
lost, and freed again.

99
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:50,890
New inventions change the battlefield: energy
shields that stop any fast-moving

100
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,990
weapon, and ships that
can fold space itself.

101
00:05:54,550 --> 00:05:59,910
But behind the banners, Iblis is building
something else: a secret police,

102
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:04,670
a ruling council, and a holy
war that answers only to him.

103
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:09,150
After almost forty years,
the League is exhausted.

104
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:13,750
The machines offer a truce, and
the people want to accept it.

105
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:19,090
For Serena and Iblis, peace with
the machines means a slow defeat.

106
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,970
So they make a terrible plan.

107
00:06:24,570 --> 00:06:27,640
Serena travels to Corrin, the
capital of the machines,

108
00:06:27,810 --> 00:06:29,460
as an ambassador of peace.

109
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:32,400
In secret, she has come to give her life.

110
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:35,880
She defies Omnius until it condemns her.

111
00:06:36,350 --> 00:06:38,720
But Erasmus sees the smile on her face.

112
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:42,770
He knows she wants this, and
he refuses to grant it.

113
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:46,620
So her most loyal guardian does
what the machines will not.

114
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:51,510
Serena Butler's end comes swiftly,
from a human hand.

115
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:55,670
Then Iblis Ginjo makes sure the
galaxy sees something else.

116
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:00,630
Images reach Salusa: Serena, suffering
at the hands of a machine.

117
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:03,390
Her remains are found,
and the cells match.

118
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:06,010
It is a clone, grown in secret.

119
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,230
The images are a lie.

120
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:11,110
And the lie works.

121
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,890
The peace movement dies overnight.

122
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:17,240
The Jihad roars back to life.

123
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:24,990
That same year, Xavier Harkonnen uncovers
the Grand Patriarch's darkest

124
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,610
secret.

125
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:28,650
To replace the organs of wounded soldiers,

126
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:33,630
Iblis and his Tlulaxa allies have been
kidnapping humans from free worlds,

127
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,170
and blaming the machines.

128
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:39,590
Xavier knows he will never reach
home alive with the truth.

129
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:43,110
So he takes the controls
of Iblis Ginjo's ship,

130
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:47,920
and flies it into a star, carrying
them both to their deaths.

131
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:52,200
But the story told afterwards
is not the truth.

132
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:56,580
Iblis becomes a martyr, the
third saint of the Jihad,

133
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:58,660
beside Serena and her son.

134
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:03,200
And Xavier Harkonnen is remembered
as a traitor and a murderer.

135
00:08:04,050 --> 00:08:07,180
His family abandons the
Harkonnen name in shame.

136
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:11,360
Only Vorian Atreides knows
what really happened.

137
00:08:12,230 --> 00:08:13,460
Remember that name.

138
00:08:13,310 --> 00:08:15,690
It is coming back.

139
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:19,340
Decades pass.

140
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:25,400
Then, in 108 BG, Omnius strikes
with a new weapon: a plague,

141
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:27,100
built to kill humans.

142
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:30,980
It sweeps through the League,
and billions die.

143
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:36,720
With the League on its knees, the machine
fleet sets course for Salusa Secundus.

144
00:08:37,470 --> 00:08:41,480
Vorian Atreides answers with the
most ruthless plan of the war.

145
00:08:42,410 --> 00:08:47,140
While the machine fleet is away,
humanity's ships fold space,

146
00:08:46,990 --> 00:08:50,780
and strike every undefended
machine world at once,

147
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:52,440
with atomics.

148
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:54,780
It is called the Great Purge.

149
00:08:55,390 --> 00:09:00,500
World after world is burned to slag,
and every human slave on them dies

150
00:09:00,350 --> 00:09:01,380
with the machines.

151
00:09:02,030 --> 00:09:03,740
Only one world survives.

152
00:09:04,450 --> 00:09:06,260
Corrin, the home of Omnius.

153
00:09:07,010 --> 00:09:09,300
The League surrounds it with a blockade,

154
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,620
and declares the Jihad over.

155
00:09:12,030 --> 00:09:16,320
For twenty years, the last of
the machines wait behind it.

156
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:22,570
In 88 BG, the Army of Humanity
comes for Corrin.

157
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,790
Vorian Atreides leads it.

158
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,450
He has already destroyed
the last of the Titans,

159
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,190
his own father among them.

160
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:32,290
At his side is Abulurd, Xavier's grandson.

161
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:37,690
Vorian has told him the truth, and Abulurd
has taken back the name Harkonnen.

162
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,830
Erasmus has prepared one final defence.

163
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:46,090
Around the planet, he has strung two
million human captives in cargo pods,

164
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:49,050
rigged to explode the moment
the fleet crosses them.

165
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:51,830
The machines call humans hrethgir.

166
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,030
This is the Bridge of Hrethgir.

167
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,350
Vorian gives the order to advance.

168
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,630
Abulurd begs him not to.

169
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,430
Then he does the unthinkable.

170
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,310
He disables the weapons
of the entire fleet.

171
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,140
The pods never explode.

172
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:10,090
Erasmus himself has switched them off,
to save the one human he cares about.

173
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,770
But no one in the fleet knows that.

174
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:16,510
Without its weapons, the battle
becomes far bloodier.

175
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:21,040
Corrin falls to atomics and to
a final assault on the ground.

176
00:10:21,770 --> 00:10:23,240
Omnius is destroyed.

177
00:10:23,930 --> 00:10:26,480
The age of thinking machines is over.

178
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,250
After the victory, Abulurd
is spared execution.

179
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:35,650
Instead, Vorian has him branded a coward,

180
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:38,770
and exiled to the frozen
world of Lankiveil,

181
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,050
forced to carry the name
Harkonnen forever.

182
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:45,490
And Vorian swears that every Atreides
will spit on that name.

183
00:10:45,890 --> 00:10:48,040
That oath will outlive empires.

184
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:52,460
Ten thousand years later, it
will end in fire on Arrakis.

185
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:57,120
Abulurd's brother Faykan takes a new
name from the battle: Corrino.

186
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:02,220
His family will sit on the Golden Lion
Throne for ten thousand years.

187
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:08,060
And humanity writes one commandment into
its holy law: Thou shalt not make

188
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:10,660
a machine in the likeness of a human mind.

189
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:14,740
Without thinking machines, humans
must become the machines.

190
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:16,520
Mentats who compute.

191
00:11:17,370 --> 00:11:18,980
Sisters who plan across centuries.

192
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:21,760
Navigators who fold space with spice.

193
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:26,440
Every power of the Imperium grows
from the ashes of this war.

194
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:30,310
And from a mother, a balcony, and a child.

195
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:35,660
So, was Vorian right to give
that order at Corrin,

196
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,320
or was Abulurd the real hero?

197
00:11:38,970 --> 00:11:40,740
Tell us what you think in the comments.

198
00:11:41,190 --> 00:11:44,280
If this story stayed with you,
give the video a like,

199
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:46,280
and subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

200
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,530
The archive is always open.
